WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:26.640
To load a 1911, the magazine release is pressed,&nbsp;
allowing the magazine to drop out of the pistol.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.084
Rounds are loaded and held under&nbsp;
the force of the magazine spring.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.288
It's then inserted into the magwell&nbsp;
and secured by the magazine catch.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.240
To chamber the first round, the&nbsp;
slide is pulled to the rear,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.798
cocking the hammer and compressing the&nbsp;
recoil spring.

00:00:52.727 --> 00:00:56.372
As the slide is released,&nbsp;the bottom edge of the breech face

00:00:56.372 --> 00:00:59.838
 strips the&nbsp;top cartridge and feeds it into the chamber.

00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:08.791
After the cartridge is chambered, the slide pushes&nbsp;
the barrel forward.

00:01:09.518 --> 00:01:13.728
The barrel pivots forward and&nbsp;up on the barrel link.

00:01:14.348 --> 00:01:18.000
The locking lugs on&nbsp;the barrel 
enter the recesses in the slide,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.272
locking the barrel to the slide.

00:01:21.774 --> 00:01:27.081
With&nbsp;the hammer cocked and the barrel locked,&nbsp;
the 1911 is ready to fire.

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:31.816
 The grip safety&nbsp;prevents rearward movement of the trigger.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.629
When firmly grasped, the trigger can be pulled.

00:01:36.725 --> 00:01:39.680
The trigger bar presses against the disconnector,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.680
transferring movement to the sear.

00:01:42.051 --> 00:01:46.395
The&nbsp;sear rotates and disengages 
the full cock notch on the hammer.

00:01:48.087 --> 00:01:50.832
 The mainspring pushes&nbsp;up on the hammer strut,

00:01:50.832 --> 00:01:54.216
rotating the hammer&nbsp;forward to strike the firing pin.

00:01:54.216 --> 00:01:58.548
 The firing&nbsp;pin travels forward, impacting the cartridge&nbsp;primer.

00:01:59.132 --> 00:02:04.000
The expanding gases from the powder&nbsp;
charge propel the bullet through the barrel.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.746
The recoil forces the slide back, and the barrel&nbsp;to unlock.

00:02:10.949 --> 00:02:14.321
The extractor grips the rim of the&nbsp;
spent cartridge case

00:02:14.321 --> 00:02:16.107
extracting it from the&nbsp;chamber.

00:02:17.359 --> 00:02:21.952
As the slide continues to the rear,&nbsp;
the casing makes contact with the ejector,

00:02:21.952 --> 00:02:24.105
 
forcing it through the ejection port.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:33.520
As the slide comes back, the hammer is cocked, 
and&nbsp;the hammer strut again compresses the mainspring.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.581
The sear spring presses against the sear,&nbsp;
which bears against the hammer.

00:02:39.164 --> 00:02:41.899
 The sear&nbsp;first passes the half cock notch,

00:02:41.899 --> 00:02:46.117
which acts as a&nbsp;fail-safe in the unlikely event 
of the full cock notch failing.

00:02:47.011 --> 00:02:51.431
It then engages the full cock&nbsp;notch, 
holding it in the cocked position.

00:02:55.386 --> 00:03:00.287
The disconnector prevents the sear from releasing&nbsp;
the hammer while the trigger is squeezed.

00:03:00.883 --> 00:03:06.000
The sear spring pushes the disconnector&nbsp;
into its upward position when releasing&nbsp;the trigger.

00:03:06.504 --> 00:03:10.071
This allows the&nbsp;1911 to be fired once again.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.120
When the hammer is cocked, 
the&nbsp;thumb safety can be engaged,

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.442
preventing rearward movement of the slide.

00:03:21.884 --> 00:03:25.278
On the inside portion of the thumb&nbsp;safety, 
is a stud.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:29.600
The stud prevents&nbsp;sear and hammer movement 
if the trigger is pulled.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.920
Once the final round of ammunition has been fired,

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.762
the magazine follower pushes up on the&nbsp;
slide stop, locking the slide open.

